				<td colspan="2"><span class="postbody">Well after a month of planning it we finally had enough people online to attempt our Guild raid in the Shattering Vale.
<br />

<br />
Everyone showed up on time, and there was a lot of excitement to be had. Sure the mobs would be grey, but it was our first raid.. That is excitement enough for me. But alas we were destined for defeat!
<br />

<br />
What may you ask feled our mighty force? Not a horde of monsters, not even a fiendish boss. No in the end we fell pre to shit poor coding and lackluster customer support.
<br />

<br />
Upon trying to enter the zone 2 members of the raid party were booted. We zoned out to invite them back, and once we had everyone got a message that we were locked out for 4 hours before we could try again.
<br />

<br />
It was petitioned but in typical SOE fashon the petition went unanswered.
<br />

<br />
So all in all I would have to say if this first raid was any indication how they will go in the future, we may as well not bother.</span><span class=sign><br />_________________<br />Shanar Nefandus - 18 Predator
<br />
Calaire - 17 Crusader
